{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Death entered through one man
Sorrow bound the world in [Bm7]chains
But hope was not in [G]vain
A [A7]new dawn breaks the [D]pain
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Christ has been [A]raised from the [G]dead
The [D]firstfruits of [A]those who [G]slept
[Bm7]No longer [A]lost in the [G]dark
His [Em]power is [A]not for the [D]weak
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
As in Adam we all die
So in Christ we live a[Bm7]gain
The order is clear and [G]true
[A]From the dust to the [D]sky
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Christ has been [A]raised from the [G]dead
The [D]firstfruits of [A]those who [G]slept
[Bm7]No longer [A]lost in the [G]dark
His [Em7]power is [A]not for the [D]weak
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[G]Each in their own appointed [D]time
[A]The promise stands [Bm7]firm and strong
[A6]From the [G]grave to the [D]throne
[Em7]A new life [A]is sung a[D]long
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
All will be [G]made alive
In the [A]light of His [D]way
{end_of_verse}
